# S12.1-R4 pristine orphan recovery diagnosis — 2026-10-02

## Observed state

- The canonical r4 `recover` operation stopped before a deployment attempt,
  backup or repository synchronization began.
- The private barrier journal is schema V1 and contains no tracked-worktree
  barrier payload.
- Both canonical `.git` directories are intact; neither
  `.git.s12-1-recovery` exists.
- Repository and parent owner/group/mode fields still match the V1 journal.
- Application and Control are clean. No competing Control sync, Git process,
  Git-metadata handle, tracked-file writer or exact parent-directory handle was
  present.
- Public WMS and the S11-independent health posture remained GREEN.

## Deterministic failure

The first real upgrade check rejects the repository parent with
`S12_1_REPOSITORY_PARENT_RED`: the parent and Application root carry both
`system.posix_acl_access` and `system.posix_acl_default`, while the legacy V1
upgrade intentionally permits only a safely structured access ACL. If that
condition were bypassed, a new worktree-barrier capture would independently
reject 30 clean Control paths whose recorded mode is owner-only, beginning
with `.gitignore`, as `S12_1_RECOVERY_WORKTREE_BARRIER_RED`.

The privacy-safe diagnostic evidence is bound by SHA-256:

- legacy gate reconstruction: `05345cf7534f7ed80669a6d0972063b497940a7290f7576b1208ae1815e1d845`
- path-class decomposition: `05c45932660de53108415480f8be352ffc3df5fbe3f61596fcffe2b64866cec2`

## Classification and correction

Classification: `C — R4 source/orchestration defect`.

The defect is not that the legacy ACL or owner-only modes should be weakened.
It is that recovery tries to create and install a new full barrier before it
can release a proven pre-mutation V1 journal. The correction adds a narrow
read-only recognition path for that exact pristine state. It validates journal
shape, current metadata, canonical Git layout, indexes, clean identities and
all relevant writer/handle exclusions around filesystem synchronization. All
classifier Git reads use the isolated recovery Git environment with optional
locking, hooks, fsmonitor, maintenance, credentials and network protocols
disabled. Before the final validation, the controller installs continuous Git
metadata and tracked-worktree mutation guards; the worktree guard also denies
external write opens. Both guards remain live through the durable journal
unlink and cross ordered inotify shutdown barriers before recovery returns.
The controller releases only the journal. No repository xattr, ACL, mode,
ownership, Git metadata or tracked content is changed.

All non-pristine and post-mutation states retain the existing full barrier
recovery unchanged. Yoti remains Sandbox-only and all production/adult/payment
gates remain closed.
